    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the elite 87.42 efficiency score for **Yordan Alvarez**. Facing a favorable matchup against Klassen (xERA 6.12), **Yordan Alvarez** stands out as the cornerstone of our lineup, bolstered by an elite 0.461 xwOBA. We are also leaning heavily into the top-of-the-order potential provided by **Kyle Schwarber** (71.83) and **Trea Turner** (71.04). Both benefit significantly from leading off or hitting second against Gibson, whose 4.19 xERA presents a prime opportunity for high-volume scoring. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (69.43) sits as our utility play, his massive 16% park factor adjustment against Rod\u00f3n makes him a high-upside gamble that the optimizer clearly prefers over the marginal reliability of middle-tier starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was keeping **Jacob Gonzalez** (50.58) out of the starting nine. While **Jacob Gonzalez** posted a respectable score driven by favorable platoon dynamics, he ultimately lacked the ceiling of **Hector Rodriguez** (51.71), whose park and platoon factors narrowly edged him out for the final outfield spot. We are also monitoring **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (59.31) closely; his aggressive base-running environment\u2014specifically the 87% SB potential against the opposing starter\u2014is a primary driver of his inclusion, even as he faces a slight risk from a -15% dynamic platoon adjustment.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our lineup pending status for both **Yordan Alvarez** and **Christian Yelich** (53.26). While we have projected them in the #2 and #6 spots respectively, any downward shift in order could dampen their efficiency. **Christian Yelich** specifically remains a moderate concern; while his 53.26 score keeps him in the mix, his -13% SP skill penalty against Bryce Miller serves as a reminder that we are riding his platoon advantage rather than raw dominance. We are prepared to adjust if the confirmed lineups shift our expected order for **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, but for now, the Zebras are positioned to maximize R and RBI potential while hunting stolen base opportunities.",
